      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the last three digits of \\(3^{12000}\\), we need to determine \\(3^{12000} \\mod 1000\\). We are given that \\(3^{400} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{1000}\\). This tells us that the order of 3 modulo 1000 is 400. Therefore, we can express \\(3^{12000}\\) in terms of \\(3^{400}\\).\n\nFirst, we note that:\n\\[3^{12000} = (3^{400})^{30}.\\]\nSince \\(3^{400} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{1000}\\), we have:\n\\[(3^{400})^{30} \\equiv 1^{30} \\pmod{1000}.\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[1^{30} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{1000}.\\]\nThus, the last three digits of \\(3^{12000}\\) are \\(\\boxed{001}\\).",
